            <ArticleTitle>Differential diagnosis of orofacial pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>627-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The successful diagnosis of orofacial pain depends on the following: 1. An accurate and detailed history of the pain 2. A detailed clinical examination of the face and associated organs 3. A thorough knowledge of those conditions that may produce facial pain In regard to the last requirement, Sir William Osler's maxim should always be remembered &quot;What you don't know--you won't diagnose.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
